cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ros2-px4-uav-autonomy: modular sense-plan-act autonomy for a ROS 2 / PX4 UAV in forest terrain"
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it."
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/ahmxtt/ros2-px4-uav-autonomy"
abstract: >-
  Deterministic 2D grid planning, clearance-validated cubic B-spline trajectory
  refinement, PX4 Offboard execution and local region-of-interest replanning
  with rejoin, for a multirotor UAV in cluttered forest terrain.

  What this release demonstrates, and what it does not. The offline planning
  chain and the local-replanning geometry are publicly reproducible: the
  occupancy grid and the A* cell path reproduce exactly, the refined trajectory
  and its derived metrics within documented numerical tolerances. Curated
  evidence from controlled PX4 SITL runs with Gazebo Harmonic is included, but
  those runs were recorded with the private development tree and are single
  measurements rather than repeated trials. The refactored public runtime has
  not completed an end-to-end armed mission: it arms, enters Offboard and holds
  position, then aborts on a telemetry-freshness watchdog before entering the
  mission phase.

  No custom SLAM or sensor-fusion method; state estimation is PX4 EKF2. No
  real-flight validation. Not safety-certified.
keywords:
  - unmanned aerial vehicle
  - path planning
  - A-star
  - B-spline trajectory
  - ROS 2
  - PX4
  - Gazebo
  - obstacle avoidance
  - reproducibility
authors:
